/* func_level_5_8007B68C (0x8007B68C, level_5_artisans_sunny_flight overlay).
 *
 * Flight-level end-of-run results/time-attack screen draw. First frame
 * (D_800758B8 == 0): runs the render pipeline once, then captures the frame
 * into VRAM strips (4x MoveImage columns + LoadImage of the backdrop strip
 * and CLUT row). Later frames: rebuilds the frozen backdrop as 4 POLY_FT4
 * quads (clut 0x3820) plus a black TILE bar, then draws either the results
 * board (COMPLETED/QUIT/TIME IS UP/CRASHED headline, four tally rows
 * revealed by D_80075744, bonus column, TOTAL, PRESS-TO-CONTINUE or
 * TRY AGAIN?/YES/NO menu) or, at D_80075744 == 0x64, the TIME ATTACK board
 * (times via the formatter D_800758C4, NEW RECORD, TRY AGAIN/YES/NO).
 * Selected records get a sine glow on +0x46 from D_8006CC78. Standard
 * 2-vblank pace tail. Word-identical in all five flight overlays
 * (5/11/17/23/29 -- x5 payoff: 32,200 bytes; fingerprint md5 confirmed
 * 2026-08-23-1).
 *
 * STATE 2026-08-27-1: length-exact (1610/1610), LINKS, and the linked diff is
 * **10 differing insns over 2 regions (99.4%)**, down from 35 over 4 (97.8%),
 * 51, then 109 in the three sessions before. The FRAME is exact (`vars= 96,
 * regs= 7/0`). R1 (21 insns), the h/strip delay-slot pair, the `img` la and
 * R3' all fell to ONE new lever this session -- LEVER 7, the do/while(0)
 * BLOCK SPLIT. What is left is R5 (5) and Rq (5), and both now have a named
 * mechanism and a measured cost, below.
 * Drive this park off BOTH the linked diff AND the shape diff -- the shape
 * diff (below) works when the length changes and the link fails, which the
 * linked differ cannot do, and it collapses the positional shift so 35 linked
 * mismatches read as the 14 insns that are actually misplaced.
 *
 * ---- Measuring this park (do this first, it is the whole game) -------------
 *   uv run --project tools/open-spyro --group split -- open-spyro diff \
 *       func_level_5_8007B68C          # ~10 s, writes build/diff/*.{orig,built}.bin
 * then objdump BOTH bins with `-b binary -m mips:3000 -EL -D`, anchor register
 * names (`\b(a[0-3]|v[01]|t[0-9]|s[0-8]|at|gp|sp|fp|ra|zero)\b` -> `R\1`),
 * mask immediates, and difflib-align. Print the RUNNING OFFSET per opcode
 * region ((j2-j1)-(i2-i1) accumulated) and the count of byte-identical words.
 * A compile-only variant of the same diff (config/compile.sh ovl + objdump of
 * the .o, `<...>` symbol suffixes stripped before masking) runs without a link
 * and is the fast inner loop; finish on the linked one.
 * **Build the compile-only diff FIRST -- it is what unstuck this park.** The
 * linked differ dies (`zip() argument 2 is shorter` / `ld: cannot move location
 * counter backwards`) on any variant whose length changes, which is exactly the
 * class the last three sessions could not evaluate, and its positional column
 * diff inflates one misplaced pair into a 21-insn "region". The masked,
 * difflib-aligned version reported the same state as 14 insns over 9 regions
 * -- four independent knots -- and made a 19-position source sweep of one
 * statement a 90-second experiment. Two mask traps, both hit this session:
 * strip `<sym>` suffixes BEFORE collapsing whitespace or every `jal` differs,
 * and anchor register names before masking immediates (a[0-3]/v[01] ARE hex).
 *
 * **The positional trap (cost this park ~5,000 bytes of credit for months).**
 * `open-spyro partial` credit is positional, so ONE unbalanced insert inside
 * the quad loop pushed the running offset to +1 for insns 145..1432 -- 1,287
 * words -- and every one of them scored zero even though the content was
 * right. The masked mismatch count did not show it (34 vs 37 either way).
 * ALWAYS check the running offset before optimising the mismatch count: a
 * source form with MORE mismatches but a ZERO offset is worth 5x more.
 *
 * ---- The four levers that took it 228 -> 1501 (2026-08-23-1) ---------------
 * 1. **Per-access `volatile` is an allocation/scheduling dial.** The quad loop
 *    writes a POLY_FT4 through `p` and reads fields back; every access was
 *    volatile to stop cse folding. Dropping `volatile` from just TWO of the
 *    ~30 accesses -- `bq = *(p + 0xD)` and `cq = *(p + 0xC)`, the two byte
 *    copy-reads -- and from `*(p + 0x12) = bh`, re-tiled the whole loop's
 *    register map onto the original's (bh/ch a1/a2, bq/cq reusing them, tpage
 *    a3 instead of t0) and closed R6 + R7 (~26 insns) outright. Sweep it
 *    per-OCCURRENCE, greedily, one `volatile ` deletion at a time (a
 *    per-offset sweep merges the store and the read-back of the same field and
 *    hides the win).
 * 2. **`allclear = 0;` above `env = D_80076EE0;`** (else-branch head). Both are
 *    priority-1 stragglers; with `env` first, its `la` won the bubble before
 *    the `lw cur`, leaving a load-delay `nop` and pushing the `bne` one slot
 *    late -- which is what created the +1 offset for the next 1,300 insns.
 *    This single statement swap took the park 215 -> 1382 identical words.
 * 3. **The permuter's `allclear = 0x15;` hack is RETIRED.** It was load-bearing
 *    only against the OLD register map; with lever 1 in place the literal
 *    `p + 0x15` is strictly better (it restores `move s5,zero` in the `bne`
 *    delay slot at orig 119 -- old R4 -- and puts `addiu s1,s1,1` back at orig
 *    168). Do not reintroduce it.
 * 4. **The TIME-ATTACK `&pos` carrier is now free** (old R13, "+1 in every
 *    spelling, must be paid back"): the payback is exactly the insn that
 *    lever 3 removed. `int *pp; pp = pos;` before the TRY AGAIN call, passed
 *    to TRY AGAIN and YES (NO rematerialises `addiu a1,sp,56`) reproduces the
 *    original's `addiu s2,sp,56; move a1,s2` carrier.
 * Also folded in this session: `i += 1` moved below the MoveImage call in the
 * capture loop (old R2), `img2[0]` inlined into the LoadImage call instead of
 * an `im` temp (half of old R3), the clut store `*(p + 0xE) = 0x3820` made
 * NON-volatile and moved above the `p + 0x25` store (this is what puts
 * `li v0,14368` in the orig-195 slot, which is load-bearing for the v0/v1
 * tiling of the u/v chains), and `a + 0x80U` instead of `a + 0x80` at the two
 * byte stores (see A-new below).
 *
 * ---- LEVER 5, the closer for R8 (2026-08-26): the single-use POINTER CARRIER
 *      in the pre-branch block ------------------------------------------------
 * Shape: `f(..., pos, ...)` where `pos` is a frame array and the call sits in a
 * MERGE block after an `if`. expand emits the arg setup (`addiu a1,sp,56`, or
 * `move a1,s2` when a carrier is already live) in the CALL block; the original
 * has it in the PRE-BRANCH block, usually stolen by reorg into the branch's
 * delay slot. Fix: declare a fresh pointer local used EXACTLY ONCE, assign it
 * immediately before the `if`, and pass IT:
 *      int *qq;  ...  qq = pos;  if (cond) {...}  f("NO", qq, 0x12, k);
 * The def is then a real insn in the pre-branch block; local-alloc gives the
 * pseudo `a1` on the copy preference and reload coalesces the copy away, so the
 * arg setup materialises exactly where the original has it, at zero insn cost.
 * When the value wanted is an already-live carrier (`move a1,s2`), assign from
 * the carrier instead (`q2 = pp;`) -- assigning from `pos` would rematerialise
 * `addiu a1,sp,56` and mismatch.
 * Applied at three sites here (results-board YES, TIME-ATTACK YES, TIME-ATTACK
 * NO) and worth 58 insns: 109 -> 51.
 * **This retires "statement permutation does not reach it" for this shape.**
 * The old note was right that permuting `pp = pos` among the `pos[]` stores does
 * nothing -- because the variable was already multi-ref; what was never tried is
 * a SEPARATE single-use local. Do NOT confuse it with B19 (a call-arg copy after
 * a same-block store batch), which is still unreachable: B19 has no branch.
 * Beware the opposite trap, `update_equiv_regs` (local-alloc.c): a pseudo with
 * `reg_n_refs == 2`, `reg_basic_block < 0` (def and use in different blocks) AND
 * a REG_EQUIV note has its USE rewritten to the equivalence and its DEF DELETED,
 * which puts the address back in the call block. A frame address has no
 * REG_EQUIV note, which is why the carrier survives here.
 *
 * ---- LEVER 6, the closer for the FRAME (2026-08-27): two reads of the SAME
 *      array element straddling a call cost one 8-byte reload slot ----------
 * The five tally arms each read their bonus cell TWICE -- once for the printf,
 * once for the accumulate -- with a call in between:
 *      func_80062FD4(buf, "%d", D_8006E924[k]);
 *      bonus += D_8006E924[D_8007595C * 5];
 * Because both spellings name the SAME base symbol, cse gives them one value
 * number; the pseudo is live across the call, reload un-allocates it and
 * `alter_reg` -> `assign_stack_local (mode, total_size, -1)` buys it an 8-byte
 * BLKmode slot (A127). Five such pairs + the TIME-ATTACK `D_80078618[...]`
 * pair = six slots = `vars= 104`. The original wants FIVE (`vars= 96`).
 * **The fix is to make ONE pair name two DIFFERENT base symbols.** D_8006E920,
 * 924, 928, 92C, 930 are the five int COLUMNS of one stride-5 row table (and
 * D_80078680..84 are its byte claim-flag columns), so `D_8006E924[k]` and
 * `D_8006E920[k + 1]` are the same address by two symbol names. Spelling the
 * ACCUMULATE against the neighbouring column's base:
 *      bonus += D_8006E920[D_8007595C * 5 + 1];   (== D_8006E924[k])
 * defeats the value numbering, frees exactly one slot, and costs ZERO insns
 * (1610 either way) -- `.frame` reads `vars= 96, regs= 7/0`, the target.
 *   - Which of the five arms carries it is ARBITRARY: all four of the possible
 *     single re-spellings give vars= 96 and the SAME 35/1610 linked diff (two
 *     of the four are byte-identical objects). Column 0 is used here.
 *   - Do NOT re-spell all five: that is 2 slots (`vars= 72`), a 4-slot
 *     overshoot. And do NOT make the printf read use the row base too -- with
 *     both sides on one base the pair is value-numbered again and the slot
 *     comes back (`vars= 104`).
 *   - This retires the old note's conclusion that the frame was unreachable
 *     without an 8th callee-saved register. Everything that list ruled out
 *     (`[0]`, `*(base+i)`, casts, `bonus = bonus + x`, hoisted temps,
 *     `register`, ternaries, sized decls) varies the INDEX spelling, which cse
 *     folds; only changing the BASE SYMBOL reaches it.
 * Worth 16 insns: 51 -> 35.
 *
 * ---- LEVER 7, the closer for R1 + 3 more (2026-08-27-1): a `do { } while (0)`
 *      BLOCK SPLIT pins a dep-free straggler to the slot after a call --------
 * THE most productive lever found on this function: 25 insns in four places.
 * Shape: a dep-free assignment (`la`/`li` of a constant or symbol address)
 * sits in a long straight-line block full of calls. The original has it in the
 * bubble immediately after call N; our build schedules it many insns later,
 * because within one basic block sched2 places it by PRIORITY (= its depth in
 * the call chain, via the unconditional REG_DEP_ANTI on `last_function_call`
 * -- `sched_analyze_1`'s hard-register branch subscripts `call_used_regs`
 * with the nregs loop counter `i`, not `regno + i`, so for any single-word set
 * the test is `call_used_regs[0]` == `$zero` == always true, and EVERY register
 * set in a block inherits the preceding call's priority) and NOT by source
 * order. Statement permutation therefore
 * cannot reach it: a full 19-position sweep of `envBase = D_80076EE0;` over
 * this block produced exactly two outcomes (14 or 20 shape mismatches) and
 * never moved the `la`.
 * **Fix: end a basic block right after the assignment.** `do { ... } while (0)`
 * survives to sched (it emits NOTE_INSN_LOOP_BEG/END, which split the block),
 * so the statement becomes the last insn of its own block and lands exactly
 * where the source puts it, at zero insn cost.
 *   - **Wrap from the call whose bubble you want, through the assignment.**
 *     The barrier's START matters as much as its end: `do {` at `strip = 0x200`
 *     (i.e. covering the last four calls) scores 20, at `func_800521C0` 22, at
 *     `func_8005DBC4` 22. Too small a block A and its own stragglers re-order
 *     (that is what swapped `li s4,224`/`li s2,512` between the 80019698 and
 *     800573C8 delay slots -- and note that swapping THOSE two statements in
 *     source does not swap them back: inside a block reorg fills delay slots
 *     LIFO from whatever sched emitted, so the dial is the block extent, not
 *     the statement order).
 *   - **Chain them.** A second barrier `do { func_80060030(...); img = ...; }
 *     while (0);` put the `img` `la` back after its call: 20 -> 14 shape / 20 ->
 *     14 linked. Each barrier buys one "this straggler goes after THAT call".
 *   - **It does NOT work inside the quad loop** (confirmed again: 1454/1610).
 *     Same finding as A195's wrappers -- the notes break the `goto quad` loop.
 *   - Applied here at exactly two sites (source lines ~349 and ~358).
 *
 * ---- Residue remaining (10 insns over 2 regions, 2026-08-27-1) ------------
 *   R5  126/131 `ori a1,a1,0x3e00` (the second half of the 0xFFFE3E00
 *               constant) sinks 4 insns, into the `lw v0,D_800785F0` load
 *               delay slot, in the block after `func_8005FDD8(env)`.
 *               **SOLVED in isolation, at a price -- read this before
 *               re-deriving.** LEVER 7 reaches it: hoist BOTH constants into
 *               their own barrier block, which forces the four constant insns
 *               into the four slots the original uses:
 *                   int off, bias;
 *                   do { off = 0x1C000; bias = 0xFFFE3E00; } while (0);
 *                   ... D_80075780 = D_800785E8 + off;
 *                   ... tv = D_800785F0[0] + bias;
 *               `ori a1` then lands byte-exact. The cost is that the two loads
 *               swap registers: the original puts `D_800785E8` in v1 and
 *               `D_800785F0[0]`/`tv` in v0, ours the other way, which repaints
 *               8 insns (b888..b8c4). Net 10 -> 13, so it is NOT checked in.
 *               The swap is a local-alloc qty_compare tie between two
 *               quantities of equal ref count (Q1 = {e8, e8+off} 5 refs,
 *               Q2 = {f0, tv} 5 refs) decided by live length, and it is NOT
 *               reachable by statement order: a full permutation sweep of the
 *               five statements in that block (60 legal orders, all built)
 *               bottoms out at 13 and never flips the pair. Also probed and
 *               rejected: `bias` at 3 positions without the barrier (13),
 *               a barrier per constant (16), `D_800756FC` re-read instead of
 *               `tv` (15), an `e8` int carrier (15), lengthening Q1 / short-
 *               ening Q2 (16-20). Next thing to try is a REF-COUNT dial on Q2
 *               (A195-style dummy wrappers to buy `tv` a ref), not an order.
 *   Rq  193-198 quad tail: ours emits `sb v0,36; li v0,14368; addiu v1,-33;
 *               sh v0,14; sb v1,37` where the orig has `addiu v1,-33;
 *               sb v0,36; li v0,14368; sb v1,37; sh v0,14`.
 *               **Root cause is now settled: the original's SOURCE ORDER for
 *               the three stores is 0x24, 0x25, 0xE -- not 0x24, 0xE, 0x25.**
 *               Proof: our `sh 0xE` is non-volatile and sits between two
 *               volatile stores, and a volatile MEM flushes sched's pending
 *               lists, so the non-volatile store can never be scheduled past
 *               `sb 0x25`; the emitted store order is therefore exactly the
 *               source order, in both spellings. Writing the source in the
 *               original's order ("clut-last") DOES put `sh v0,14(s0)` at
 *               b9a0 byte-exact -- and re-tiles v0/v1/a1 across the preceding
 *               24 insns (b934..b99c), for a net 10 -> 30.
 *               That re-tiling is what the whole per-access `volatile` map
 *               (LEVER 1) is currently tuned against. Searched and exhausted
 *               this session: single-removal sweep over all 30 `volatile`s
 *               (best 24), greedy multi-round removal (stops at 24), greedy
 *               ADD-or-REMOVE toggle over every access in the loop (stops at
 *               24), and `clut` hoisted to its own `li` statement (30).
 *               **Read this as the standing hypothesis: the permuter-era
 *               `volatile` scaffolding is the thing that is wrong.** The real
 *               source is almost certainly a plain POLY_FT4 struct filled
 *               field by field with no `volatile` anywhere; the scaffolding
 *               reproduces the ORDER by brute force and then cannot express
 *               the original's order here. The next serious attempt on this
 *               function should be a clean rewrite of the quad loop against a
 *               real struct, not another volatile permutation.
 *   The frame is CLOSED (was +16): `.frame $sp,144 # vars= 96, regs= 7/0`,
 *   matching the original's `addiu sp,-144`. See LEVER 6 above.
 *   CLOSED this session by LEVER 7 (all four were "unreachable" before):
 *     - R1 (21) `la envBase` 20 insns late -- barrier after `func_8005DBC4(0)`.
 *     - the `li s4,224`/`li s2,512` delay-slot swap the first barrier
 *       introduced -- fixed by moving the barrier's START to `strip = 0x200`.
 *     - the `img` `la` 4 insns early -- second barrier around
 *       `func_80060030(...); img = D_800785F0;`.
 *     - R3' (4) `lw a1,0(s3)`/`addiu a0,sp,16` arg setup below the `rect`
 *       stores in the capture loop -- **moving `strip += 0x40;` BELOW the
 *       `func_8005FA28(&rect, img2[0])` call** lets sched hoist the whole arg
 *       setup above the stores. (`s2` is callee-saved, so the increment is
 *       free after the call; the original still emits it before the `jal`.)
 *       Probed and worse: a barrier around the call (18), `rect.x` last (14),
 *       an `im` temp at any position.
 * ---- Older diagnoses that are still true ----------------------------------
 * B14 RETIRED 2026-08-06-1 (the "+1 nop / cannot link" blocker is gone): the
 * three dep-free defs (`la envBase`, `la img`, `addiu img2`) are priority-1
 * stragglers and `rank_for_schedule` breaks the tie on INSN_LUID DESCENDING,
 * i.e. source order; the current order (img, img2, envBase) is the only one of
 * the three legal orders that links.
 * R10/R11/R12 SOLVED 2026-08-20 and their recipes are still in the body: the
 * glow LUT gets its OWN pre-loop local (`short *lut = (short *) D_8006CC78;`)
 * declared immediately above `ph` so loop.c cannot hoist its `la` past the
 * preheader assignment (A93), and two nested `do { } while (0)` wrappers around
 * the publish loop's `slot += 1;` buy `slot` two refs and flip its qty_compare
 * priority against `r` (A195 reaches local-alloc's qty_compare).
 * **A195 wrappers do NOT work inside the quad loop** (re-measured
 * 2026-08-23-1, five depths on both `bq` statements): the dummy loops' NOTEs
 * split the block and cost 20-45 mismatches.
 *
 * NOTE: the body below is descended from the 2026-07-25 decomp-permuter output
 * but every construct that survives is now accounted for above.
 */

